{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/changes.patch'","aggregated_output":"--- v33/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/grid_map.h\n+++ v34/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/grid_map.h\n@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@\n #include <plan_env/reactive_collision.h>\n #include <plan_env/collision_segment.h>\r\n #include <plan_env/eth_step_score_adaptation.h>\r\n+#include <plan_env/evidence_floor_fill.h>\r\n #include <set>\r\n \r\n #define logit(x) (log((x) / (1 - (x))))\r\n@@ -247,6 +248,8 @@\n   bool reactiveTerrainReturn(const Eigen::Vector3d &point) const;\r\n   void reactiveTomogramCallback(sensor_msgs::msg::PointCloud2::ConstSharedPtr msg);\n   reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot decodeReactiveGround(sensor_msgs::msg::PointCloud2::ConstSharedPtr msg) const;\n+  // v34: the navigation ground plus the guarded evidence floor (evidence_floor_fill.h).\n+  reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot supportGround(const reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot &navigation);\n   void reactiveSurfaceGroundCallback(sensor_msgs::msg::PointCloud2::ConstSharedPtr msg);\n   bool reactiveSurfaceGroundReady() const;\r\n   inline int getLocalIndex(int id, int dim) const;\r\n@@ -291,6 +294,9 @@\n   reactive_stair::CollisionDecision reactive_decision_{reactive_parameters_};\n   reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot reactive_terrain_;\n   reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot reactive_ground_; // Unscored positive ground evidence.\n+  // v34: the navigation ground as decoded. New evidence is always applied to it,\n+  // never to reactive_ground_, which holds the augmented copy.\n+  reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot reactive_navigation_ground_;\n   // Explicit raw-return classification evidence; scored navigation support stays separate.\n   reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot reactive_surface_ground_;\n   std::string reactive_surface_ground_topic_;\n--- v33/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/scan_reactive_grid_methods.inc\n+++ v34/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/scan_reactive_grid_methods.inc\n@@ -75,12 +75,32 @@\n   return terrain;\n }\n \n+reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot GridMap::supportGround(const reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot &navigation) {\n+  // v34: PCT's navigation ground is inflated; the surface evidence is its\n+  // uninflated selection. Add the evidence floor that the navigation ground lacks,\n+  // except beside drops (audits/2026-09-29_corridor_entry, versions/v34/PLAN.md).\n+  reactive_stair::EvidenceFloorFill fill;\n+  auto ground = reactive_stair::addGuardedEvidenceFloor(navigation, &reactive_surface_ground_,\n+      reactive_parameters_.body_height_tolerance_m, reactive_stair::StepScoreParameters{}.critical_height_m,\n+      mp_.double_cylinder_radius_, &fill);\n+  size_t layers = 0;\n+  for (const auto &entry : navigation.cells) layers += entry.second.size();\n+  RCLCPP_INFO(node_->get_logger(),\n+      \"evidence_floor_fill evidence_used=%d navigation_layers=%zu added=%zu drop_rejected=%zu\",\n+      fill.evidence_used ? 1 : 0, layers, fill.added, fill.drop_rejected);\n+  return ground;\n+}\n+\n void GridMap::reactiveTomogramCallback(sensor_msgs::msg::PointCloud2::ConstSharedPtr msg) {\n   reactive_ground_ = reactive_stair::TerrainSnapshot{};\n   reactive_cloud_ready_ = false;\n   reactive_pending_cloud_ = false;\n   reactive_terrain_hits_.clear();\n   auto terrain = decodeReactiveGround(msg);\n+  // v34: keep the navigation ground as decoded, and give SCAN's copy the guarded\n+  // evidence floor. An invalid ground passes unchanged.\n+  reactive_navigation_ground_ = terrain;\n+  terrain = supportGround(terrain);\n   if (terrain.cells.empty()) {\n     reactive_decision_.acceptTerrain(terrain);\n     return;\n@@ -104,6 +124,9 @@\n   reactive_pending_cloud_ = false;\n   // The step score consults this evidence, so rescore the accepted navigation\n   // ground. Unusable evidence scores exactly as without evidence.\n+  // v34: re-augment the navigation ground as decoded with this evidence, so the\n+  // result does not depend on which message arrived first.\n+  if (!reactive_ground_.cells.empty()) reactive_ground_ = supportGround(reactive_navigation_ground_);\n   if (!reactive_ground_.cells.empty()) {\n     reactive_stair::StepScoreResult scored = reactive_stair::precomputeEthStyleStepScores(\n         reactive_ground_, {}, &reactive_surface_ground_);\n--- /dev/null\n+++ v34/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/evidence_floor_fill.h\n@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@\n+#ifndef P2B_EVIDENCE_FLOOR_FILL_H\n+#define P2B_EVIDENCE_FLOOR_FILL_H\n+\n+// v34 (Dr Sun, 2026-09-29; audits/2026-09-29_corridor_entry). SCAN's footprint\n+// support reads PCT's navigation ground, which PCT trims by its obstacle-distance\n+// inflation. The surface evidence is PCT's uninflated selection of the same\n+// ground. Where the navigation cell containing an evidence cell's centre has no\n+// layer within tolerance_m of an evidence layer, the returned ground gains that\n+// layer, unless a drop lies within guard_radius_m: an evidence cell whose square\n+// comes within guard_radius_m of the candidate's square, with no surface within\n+// step_m of the layer and either no surface at all or one more than step_m below\n+// it. A cell with only higher surfaces is solid (a wall under an upper floor);\n+// LiDAR occupancy still decides obstacles. Navigation layers are never changed or\n+// removed. Unusable evidence adds nothing, as it scores exactly as without\n+// evidence in the step score (v30).\n+#include <plan_env/reactive_collision.h>\n+\n+#include <algorithm>\n+#include <cmath>\n+#include <cstddef>\n+#include <limits>\n+#include <vector>\n+\n+namespace reactive_stair {\n+\n+struct EvidenceFloorFill {\n+  bool evidence_used = false;\n+  std::size_t added = 0;          // evidence layers added to the navigation ground\n+  std::size_t drop_rejected = 0;  // candidates rejected because a drop lies within the guard\n+};\n+\n+inline bool evidenceFillIndex(double coordinate, double origin, double resolution, int &index) {\n+  const double value = std::floor((coordinate - origin) / resolution);\n+  if (!std::isfinite(value) || value < std::numeric_limits<int>::min() ||\n+      value > std::numeric_limits<int>::max()) return false;\n+  index = static_cast<int>(value);\n+  return true;\n+}\n+\n+inline TerrainSnapshot addGuardedEvidenceFloor(const TerrainSnapshot &navigation,\n+                                               const TerrainSnapshot *evidence,\n+                                               double tolerance_m, double step_m,\n+                                               double guard_radius_m,\n+                                               EvidenceFloorFill *summary = nullptr) {\n+  TerrainSnapshot out = navigation;\n+  EvidenceFloorFill fill;\n+  const bool usable = evidence != nullptr && valid(navigation) && valid(*evidence) &&\n+      evidence->frame == navigation.frame &&\n+      std::abs(evidence->resolution_m - navigation.resolution_m) <= 1e-9 &&\n+      std::isfinite(tolerance_m) && tolerance_m >= 0.0 &&\n+      std::isfinite(step_m) && step_m > 0.0 &&\n+      std::isfinite(guard_radius_m) && guard_radius_m >= 0.0;\n+  if (!usable) {\n+    if (summary) *summary = fill;\n+    return out;\n+  }\n+  fill.evidence_used = true;\n+  const double resolution = navigation.resolution_m;\n+  // Evidence cells whose squares come within guard_radius_m of the candidate cell's square.\n+  std::vector<Cell2> guard;\n+  const int reach = static_cast<int>(std::ceil(guard_radius_m / resolution)) + 1;\n+  for (int dx = -reach; dx <= reach; ++dx)\n+    for (int dy = -reach; dy <= reach; ++dy) {\n+      const double gap_x = std::max(0, std::abs(dx) - 1) * resolution;\n+      const double gap_y = std::max(0, std::abs(dy) - 1) * resolution;\n+      if (gap_x * gap_x + gap_y * gap_y <= guard_radius_m * guard_radius_m + 1e-12)\n+        guard.push_back({dx, dy});\n+    }\n+  // A drop: no surface within step_m of the level, and no surface at all or one below it.\n+  const auto drop = [&](const Cell2 &cell, double level) {\n+    const auto found = evidence->cells.find(cell);\n+    if (found == evidence->cells.end()) return true;\n+    bool lower = false;\n+    for (const SurfaceCell &surface : found->second) {\n+      if (std::abs(surface.elevation_m - level) <= step_m) return false;\n+      if (surface.elevation_m < level - step_m) lower = true;\n+    }\n+    return lower;\n+  };\n+  for (const auto &entry : evidence->cells) {\n+    int ix = 0, iy = 0;\n+    if (!evidenceFillIndex(evidence->origin_x_m + (entry.first.x + 0.5) * resolution,\n+                           navigation.origin_x_m, resolution, ix) ||\n+        !evidenceFillIndex(evidence->origin_y_m + (entry.first.y + 0.5) * resolution,\n+                           navigation.origin_y_m, resolution, iy)) continue;\n+    const Cell2 target{ix, iy};\n+    for (const SurfaceCell &candidate : entry.second) {\n+      const double level = candidate.elevation_m;\n+      const auto present = out.cells.find(target);\n+      if (present != out.cells.end() &&\n+          std::any_of(present->second.begin(), present->second.end(), [&](const SurfaceCell &surface) {\n+            return std::abs(surface.elevation_m - level) <= tolerance_m;\n+          })) continue;\n+      bool rejected = false;\n+      for (const Cell2 &offset : guard)\n+        if (drop({entry.first.x + offset.x, entry.first.y + offset.y}, level)) {\n+          rejected = true;\n+          break;\n+        }\n+      if (rejected) {\n+        ++fill.drop_rejected;\n+        continue;\n+      }\n+      // The decoder's default status; the step score labels it with the other layers.\n+      out.cells[target].push_back({Support::Stair, level});\n+      ++fill.added;\n+    }\n+  }\n+  if (summary) *summary = fill;\n+  return out;\n+}\n+\n+}  // namespace reactive_stair\n+\n+#endif\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/PLAN.md .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/COMPONENT_RESULTS.md .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/prepared.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/PLAN.md .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/COMPONENT_RESULTS.md .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/prepared.json'","aggregated_output":"# v34: SCAN adds PCT's uninflated floor where its navigation ground lacks it, except beside drops\n\nStage: experiment + analysis. Parent: v33. Native parent: `runtime/scan64_input_refresh_v31` (v31's build, which v32\nand v33 ran unchanged).\n\n## Decision and basis\n\n- **Dr Sun, 2026-09-29, after the corridor-entry diagnosis** (`audits/2026-09-29_corridor_entry/RESULT.md`), chose\n  \"Floor fallback in SCAN\". The option as offered was a code change: where PCT's map has no usable floor at a spot,\n  SCAN may use the surface map's floor there if it is within 0.12 m of the robot's floor level. It was preferred over\n  correcting the pinned map at the two spots, or at the wrong-height cells only.\n- **The trial, same day:** a single trial on gpu5070ti, as for v33 (same runner rules, host note, abort rule and\n  retry rule).\n- **A refinement made in building v34 (reported to Dr Sun; stricter, never looser than the option as offered):** a\n  drop guard. Offline, 15,451 of the 39,999 evidence layers the navigation ground lacks lie within 0.35 m of a lower\n  level where their own level is absent. A fallback without the guard would therefore let a footprint circle sit at a\n  stairwell or opening edge, which PCT's inflation keeps clear today. The guard rejects exactly those (below).\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe diagnosis replayed v32's and v33's corridor-entry stands with the native planner and found two blockers in PCT's\npinned navigation ground (`ground_precise.f32`), both turned into planning failures by SCAN's support query:\n- **Wrong-height cells (v32):** four corridor cells carry only the landing height, 1.419 m, where the floor is\n  1.561 m. Curve samples over cell (47, 41) fail the body-cell height match by about 1 cm.\n- **A narrow entry band (v33):**\n  - **The band:** the floor band is 0.8–1.0 m wide. It ends 0.5–0.6 m short of the wall that LiDAR measures, and PCT's\n    route runs 0.04–0.17 m inside its east edge.\n  - **Why it fails:** SCAN needs both footprint-circle centres over navigation cells with a floor layer. Headings\n    within about 45° of east–west are therefore unsupported at the stand.\n  - **At v33's start:** the rebound optimizer checks its first control points there at 0° (two coincident points)\n    and at −98.96°. All three are unsupported, so SCAN reports \"The robot is inside an obstacle\".\n- **Counterfactual grounds:** fixing the four cells alone unblocks v32's stand, not v33's. Filling the entry band\n  unblocks v33's. With both fixes, both stands plan on the first attempt.\n\nThe surface evidence (`raw_ground.f32`) is PCT's own uninflated selection of the same ground (traversability cost\n≤ 20, computed on the original PCD points plus dense mesh samples, `audits/2026-09-27_dense_static_sampling`). v30\nalready lets it vouch for the ring PCT's inflation trimmed, in the step score. v34 lets it supply the floor itself\nwhere the navigation ground has none at that level.\n\n## The rule\n\nWhen SCAN accepts its ground inputs, its copy of the navigation ground gains an evidence floor layer where both\nconditions hold:\n1. **The navigation ground lacks it.** The navigation cell containing the evidence cell's centre has no layer within\n   0.12 m (`body_height_tolerance`) of the evidence layer. This includes layers the rule added earlier in the same\n   pass.\n2. **No drop lies within 0.35 m** (`double_cylinder_radius`, the footprint circle's radius). Every evidence cell whose\n   square comes within 0.35 m of the candidate cell's square is either:\n   - **floor:** it has a surface within 0.26 m (the step capability) of the layer; or\n   - **solid:** it has no such surface and none below, but a surface above (a wall under an upper floor).\n\n   A cell with a surface more than 0.26 m below the layer and none within 0.26 m of it is a drop. So is a cell with\n   no surface at all. One drop rejects the layer.\n\nThe added layer is a navigation layer like any other:\n- **Height and status:** it takes the evidence height and the decoder's default status (`Stair`) before scoring.\n- **Scoring:** the step score (v30's rule, with the same evidence) labels it with the rest.\n- **Consumers:** the support query, the decision and every planner step read the augmented ground unchanged.\n- **Unchanged:** the navigation ground's own layers are never changed or removed.\n- **Unusable evidence** adds nothing: evidence that is absent, invalid, in another frame or at another resolution\n  leaves the ground exactly as v33 had it, as v30 treats unusable evidence.\n\n**Offline effect on the pinned grounds** (a Python model of the rule; the contract's oracle is written separately):\n- **Added:** 17,214 layers in 15,899 cells: 14,458 on the ground floor (0.06 m), 1,205 on the upper floor (1.5–1.6 m)\n  and the rest higher.\n- **Rejected by the drop guard:** 22,785 candidate layers.\n- **At the entry:** rows 46–53 widen from an east edge at x −4.795 to −4.495. The measured wall face is at −4.20 to\n  −4.26.\n- **The four wrong-height cells** gain the 1.561 m floor.\n- **The static route screen** (`audits/2026-09-29_corridor_entry/route_support_margin.py`'s method): poses with less\n  than ±30° of supported heading fall from 97 to 77.\n  - The 15 narrow poses of the entry group (route poses 79–96) all clear.\n  - Recomputed after K2 with the layers scan65 actually adds (`route_screen_native.py`, `route_screen_native.json`):\n    the same 77, and none in the entry group.\n  - The rest are at the corridor's east-end corner and further on, mostly beside drops the guard keeps.\n\n## Exact change\n\n`materialize.py` copies `runtime/scan64_input_refresh_v31` to `runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34` and changes three\nfiles. It inserts lines only; it asserts that removing them gives back the scan64 bytes and keeps every line ending.\n1. **`plan_env/include/plan_env/evidence_floor_fill.h` (new):** `addGuardedEvidenceFloor(navigation, evidence,\n   tolerance, step, guard_radius, summary)`. It is a pure function, the rule above.\n2. **`plan_env/include/plan_env/grid_map.h`:**\n   - includes the new header;\n   - adds the member `reactive_navigation_ground_`, the navigation ground as decoded, kept so that new evidence is\n     always applied to the original and never to an augmented copy.\n3. **`plan_env/include/plan_env/scan_reactive_grid_methods.inc`:** the two ground callbacks.\n   - **The tomogram callback:** keeps the decoded navigation ground, augments it with the current evidence, scores\n     the result (v30's rule), and on acceptance stores the augmented ground as the raw ground and its scores as the\n     terrain.\n   - **The surface callback:** re-augments the kept navigation ground with the new evidence and rescores it, so the\n     result does not depend on message order.\n   - **A log line** gives the added and rejected counts.\n\nThe planner YAML files are v33's copies, unchanged. Every other byte of the native tree is scan64's.\n\n## Preserved\n\n- **Inputs:** the pinned navigation ground and surface evidence bytes, and their publishers.\n- **Queries:** the step score and its evidence rule and parameters; the support query and `CollisionDecision::decide`\n  (code and thresholds); the body clearance and height tolerance; the known-footprint waiver; the LiDAR occupancy and\n  inflation; and the stale, missing, out-of-map and map-boundary verdicts.\n- **Planner:** the frontier walk, A*, the optimizer, all manager gates, the FSM and its replan limit; the controller,\n  executor and emergency hold.\n- **The rest of the stack:** v33's simulation-time pose gate and backstop, the backend, the bridge and the Newton\n  worker; PCT's route.\n\n## Acceptance plan and expected signals\n\n1. **K1: materialization and build.**\n   - Byte-exact insertion (removing the inserted lines gives back scan64, per file); `changes.patch` applied to\n     `parent_source/` reproduces the three files.\n   - A build in the pinned image from the scan64 colcon cache, with source identity checked before and after.\n   - The recompiled translation units, changed installed files and warnings are listed against scan64.\n2. **K2: the red/green fill contract** (`fill_contract/`).\n   - **Builds:** one source is compiled against scan64 (red) and scan65 (green).\n   - **Header part (green only):** the header does not exist in red. Synthetic cases:\n\n     | Case | Expected (green) |\n     |---|---|\n     | Band trimmed beside a wall (only higher surfaces beyond) | floor added up to the solid cells |\n     | Isolated wrong-height cell inside a floor | floor added; the wrong layer kept |\n     | Lower level 0.30 m away (inside the guard) | not added |\n     | Lower level just beyond the guard (square distance > 0.35 m) | added |\n     | Neighbour with no surface at all inside the guard | not added |\n     | Navigation layer within 0.12 m | not added |\n     | Navigation layer 0.13 m away | added beside it |\n     | Evidence absent, another frame, another resolution, empty or non-finite | nothing added; output equals input |\n     | Evidence origin offset by a sub-cell amount | added in the navigation cell containing each evidence centre |\n     | Duplicate candidates for one navigation cell | added once |\n\n   - **Real map:** green's added layer set on the pinned grounds equals an independent Python implementation of the\n     rule (`fill_contract/oracle.py`) exactly, and the navigation layers are all kept.\n   - **Node, both builds:** delivery orders navigation then evidence, evidence then navigation, then malformed\n     evidence, then valid evidence again.\n     - **Green:** the node's raw ground and terrain must equal the header result for the evidence currently usable,\n       and never include layers added for superseded evidence.\n     - **Red:** the node's must equal the navigation ground scored as scan64 scores it.\n3. **K3: the two frozen corridor-entry stands** (`audits/2026-09-29_corridor_entry/{v32,v33}_stand`).\n   - **The probe:** `corridor_probe` rebuilt against scan65, with the pinned grounds.\n   - **Expected (green):** both stands' live entry plans on the first attempt, and the committed curve passes the\n     native full check.\n   - **Red:** the audit's records, which reproduce both live failures.\n4. **K4: saved states and native regression.**\n   - **Suites:** v31's saved-state suite (`runs/v31_saved_states02`'s inputs) and complete native regression suite\n     (`runs/v31_native_regression03`'s inputs), on scan65, with no other container on the Docker VM.\n   - **Comparison:** outputs are compared with scan64's recorded outputs. Every difference is explained before\n     freezing, not waived.\n   - **Differences are expected** where added floor changes support: candidate sets, seeds, attempt sequences and\n     accepted curves.\n   - **The 8 measured obstacle cases** must keep their verdicts, and the drop and wrong-level negatives must hold.\n5. **K5: independent review.** A read-only review of the change, the contract and the evidence.\n6. **Freeze, then one physical trial on gpu5070ti** (`PHYSICAL_RUN_PLAN.md`, written before the freeze).\n   - **The run:** the historical full route with v33's profile, with `--native-build runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34`\n     and `--integration-version v34`.\n   - **Expected:** no stand at the corridor entry from either blocker.\n   - **Not expected to change:** the tight windows at the corridor's east-end corner and further on, which lie beside\n     drops the guard keeps.\n\n## Claim boundary and residual risk\n\n- **What support now means.** v34 changes what SCAN treats as supported ground. Where PCT's inflation trimmed floor,\n  SCAN's footprint may now stand on it, and walls there are left to SCAN's LiDAR occupancy, as v30 already left\n  them for the step score.\n- **The drop guard's residual:** it reads only the evidence.\n  - A cell with no surface at its level and nothing below, but a surface above, is taken as solid. An opening above\n    ground that PCT's uninflated selection also excludes would be taken for a wall; LiDAR does not see voids.\n  - The guard covers the footprint circle: evidence cells within 0.35 m of the cell's square. A drop farther away is\n    not guarded by v34; there the navigation ground's own layers and PCT's inflation margin are unchanged.\n- **The evidence is not bound to the map** beyond frame and resolution (as in v30). In simulation both grounds come\n  from one Building; real-robot use would need both from the real map.\n- **Ground-floor additions** (14,458 layers) change support before the stairs too. Start and approach behaviour may\n  differ from v33's.\n- **The added layers are scored like navigation layers.** Next to a wall the step score may leave an added edge layer\n  `Unknown`, which blocks as before.\n- **Not addressed:**\n  - the 0° heading of coincident start control points;\n  - the replan start at the executing curve's end;\n  - the 1,000-replan limit;\n  - the tight corners beyond the corridor entry.\n- **Labels.** Only a physical run can support a navigation claim. A version increment is not acceptance, and v3 remains\n  the last accepted condition.\n# v34 component results (scan65)\n\nThese are acceptance steps K1–K4 of `PLAN.md`, on `runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34`. All ran in this MacBook's\nDocker VM with the pinned Humble image, and no physical episode had run when they were recorded. K5, the\nindependent review, is recorded separately.\n\n## K1: materialization and build\n\n- **Byte-exact materialization** (`materialize.py`, `changes.patch`, `check_build.py` → `check_build.json`):\n  - **What changed:** 144 lines inserted, none removed, in three files:\n    - the new header `evidence_floor_fill.h`: +115;\n    - `grid_map.h`: +6;\n    - `scan_reactive_grid_methods.inc`: +23.\n  - **Removal check:** removing the insertions gives back scan64's bytes, file by file.\n  - **Line endings:** `grid_map.h` mixes CRLF and LF (433 of 516 lines CRLF). Its first insertion follows a CRLF line\n    and is CRLF; the other two follow LF lines.\n  - **Patch check:** applying `changes.patch` to `parent_source/` (scan64's bytes) and to an empty file reproduces\n    all three scan65 files byte for byte. Every other source file equals scan64's.\n- **Build** (`repairs/2026-09-26_generic_occupancy/build_candidate.py`):\n  - **Result:** built scan65 in the pinned image from scan64's colcon cache in 129 s. It passed, and the source\n    identity was unchanged before and after. Evidence: `build_evidence_scan65_evidence_floor_v34/` and\n    `candidate65_evidence_floor_v34_identity.json`.\n  - **A first attempt did not start** (`attempt01_docker_daemon_down/`): Docker Desktop was not running, and no\n    container ran.\n- **What recompiled:** the same 7 translation units as v31's build: `grid_map.cpp`, `dyn_a_star.cpp`,\n  `bspline_optimizer.cpp`, `measured_cloud_probe.cpp`, `scan_planner_node.cpp`, `scan_replan_fsm.cpp` and\n  `planner_manager.cpp`.\n- **Installed files that changed from scan64:**\n  - `libplan_env.a`, `scan_planner_node` and `measured_cloud_probe`;\n  - the headers `grid_map.h` and `scan_reactive_grid_methods.inc`, and the new `evidence_floor_fill.h`.\n\n  `libbspline_opt.a`, `libpath_searching.a` and every shared library are byte-identical to scan64's.\n- **Warnings:** 32 in both builds, the same multiset of file, line, column and message. None is new, and none names\n  the new code.\n\n## K2: the red/green fill contract (`fill_contract/`)\n\n- **Setup:**\n  - **Builds:** one source is compiled against scan64 (red, `red_v33/`, 104 s) and scan65 (green, `green_v34/`,\n    126 s). All exit codes are 0.\n  - **The rule's parameters:** tolerance 0.12 m, step 0.26 m, guard radius 0.35 m.\n  - **The oracle:** `oracle.py` is an independent Python implementation of `PLAN.md`'s rule. `check.py` judges both\n    builds against it (`contract_results.json`: passed).\n- **Synthetic cases (16, `make_cases.py`).** Red returns every input unchanged. Green equals the oracle layer by\n  layer, and each case's designed outcome holds on both the oracle's and the native output:\n\n  | Case | Green |\n  |---|---|\n  | Band trimmed beside solid cells | all 195 trimmed floor cells added |\n  | Isolated wrong-height cell | the floor added at that cell only; the wrong layer kept first |\n  | Lower level at (15, 6) inside the guard | 1.56 m not added within 0.35 m (square to square) of it; 126 added elsewhere, plus the hole's own lower layer |\n  | No surface at all at (15, 6) | the same rejection set; 126 added |\n  | Only a higher surface at (15, 6) (solid) | nothing rejected for it; 194 added |\n  | A surface 0.20 m below at (15, 6) | floor for the guard; nothing rejected |\n  | A surface 0.27 m below at (15, 6) | a drop; the same rejections as a lower level |\n  | Navigation layer 0.10 m from the evidence floor | nothing added at the floor |\n  | Navigation layer 0.13 m away | the floor added beside it in every trimmed cell |\n  | Two evidence layers 0.04 m apart | added once per cell |\n  | Evidence origin offset by −0.07 m | each layer added in the navigation cell containing its evidence cell's centre |\n  | Evidence absent, in another frame or resolution, empty, or non-finite | nothing added; output equals input |\n\n- **Real map** (the pinned grounds):\n  - **Green:** adds 17,214 layers and rejects 22,785 candidates near drops, exactly the oracle's set (cell and\n    float64 height). Every navigation layer is kept. The navigation ground has 27,278 cells; the result has 28,378.\n  - **Red:** adds nothing.\n  - **By height:** 14,458 of the added layers are on the ground floor (0.1 m bin) and 1,205 on the upper floor\n    (1.5–1.6 m).\n  - **Scoring:** after v30's step score, the added layers are 14,915 Flat, 445 Stair and 1,854 Unknown; Unknown still\n    blocks.\n  - **Cost:** one full-map fill takes 63 ms, best of three.\n- **Node** (`fill_order_contract`, real subscriptions, both builds). Two orders:\n  - **navigation first:** navigation, evidence, malformed evidence, evidence again, navigation again, evidence with\n    a hole east of the entry band, evidence again;\n  - **evidence first:** evidence, then navigation.\n\n  At every checkpoint (7 and 2), in both builds, the node's raw ground, its scored terrain and the decision's terrain\n  equal the tree's own headers applied to the node's decoded inputs with the evidence then usable. Green's kept\n  navigation ground equals the decoded navigation ground.\n  - **Green adds:** none without usable evidence; 17,214 with the pinned evidence; 17,177 with the hole.\n  - **The hole:** it removes 4 evidence floor points, one per cell in x −4.495 to −4.395, y −3.55 to −3.15. Those\n    cells keep only the ground floor below and the upper floors, so 37 added layers within 0.35 m of them are rejected\n    as beside a drop.\n  - **Red:** never adds.\n\n## K3: the two frozen corridor-entry stands (`stand_replay/`)\n\n- **The replay:** the corridor-entry audit's `corridor_probe`, rebuilt against scan65, on the audit's frozen states\n  with the pinned grounds.\n- **v32's state:** it is the audit's re-frozen one, at its live replan moment (audit review round 1, B2). The run on\n  the first, 5 ms late state is kept in `attempt01_v32_late/`, and it gave the same outcome (a 5.84 s clear curve on\n  the first attempt).\n\n| Stand | scan64 (the audit's replay; reproduces the trial) | scan65 |\n|---|---|---|\n| v33 | 9 failed attempts: \"inside an obstacle\" at the start, then seed and optimizer failures | the first attempt plans; the committed 5.47 s curve to (−1.658, −4.144) passes the native full check (548 samples) |\n| v32 | 9 failed attempts: curves rejected at cell (47, 41) | the first attempt plans; the committed 5.77 s curve to the same target passes (578 samples) |\n\n- **Headings:** all start headings are free at both stands on scan65.\n- **Cross-check:** the probe's breakdown matched the native functions, with 0 mismatches.\n- **The fill's log lines:** each replay's six `evidence_floor_fill` lines include the used-evidence ones, with\n  86,775 navigation layers, 17,214 added and 22,785 rejected.\n\n## K4: saved states and native regression\n\nBoth suites are v31's, rebuilt against scan65. Each ran alone on the Docker VM (`alone_check.json`: 0 samples with\nanother container). Every output and normalised log is compared with scan64's recorded run.\n- **`log_review.py`:** keeps v31's normalisation and also drops v34's `evidence_floor_fill` lines, recorded\n  separately.\n- **`difference_analysis.py`:** checks every query-CSV change against the fill. It also sorts the log differences by\n  kind.\n\n### Saved states (`runs/v34_saved_states01`, 498 s; `review.json`: component scope passed)\n\n- **Exit codes:** all 9 probes and both breakdowns exit 0.\n- **Every state still continues**, with the same frontier.\n- **The seven walking-start states:**\n  - `result.json` and `result_negatives.json` are identical to v31's.\n  - Their query CSVs differ only in `front_support_count` and `rear_support_count` (957 of 1,474 rows). In every row\n    each count grows by exactly the layers the fill added in that footprint cell.\n- **Landing and onset (the v29 landing-stall states, on the upper landing)** accept longer continuations:\n  - landing: 0.568 → 0.914 m;\n  - onset: 1.401 → 1.833 m.\n\n  Their local target moves into the corridor, from (−4.86, −3.65) and (−4.91, −3.46) to (−4.42, −4.14) and (−4.43,\n  −4.13). 9 and 3 route samples at the corridor entry (x −5.0 to −4.2, y −4.3 to −3.5) turn from blocked to free,\n  each with a footprint circle or body cell over a cell where the fill added the floor. The landing probe's breakdown\n  outputs follow.\n- **Logs:**\n  - **`reactive_collision_blocked`:** the same lines except the terrain cell count (27,278 → 28,378).\n  - **`near_sensor_verdict`:** the diagnostic prints the first queried voxels near the sensor, and only those that\n    pass support. The printed set follows the query order. At landing and onset, v34 prints 3 and 2\n    measured-obstacle verdicts at points east of the old band edge, which now reach the LiDAR check.\n  - **Optimizer and A* lines:** they differ where support changed the candidate sets. Where a start state's A*\n    recovered a connector, the connector and cost are the same.\n\n### Native regression (`runs/v34_native_regression01`, 464 s; `review.json`: component scope passed)\n\n- **Continuations:** all 11 are accepted with full gates and negatives. Their JSON outputs and negatives are\n  identical to v31's, and the four repeats are identical.\n- **Contracts:** the body-support contract (15 cases) and the ground contract pass.\n- **Obstacle cases:** all 8 unmapped measured cases (empty, static human, box, thin wall, post, low box, occluded\n  human, blocked corridor) and all 5 mapped cases give output identical to v31's.\n- **Query CSVs:** all 11 differ only in the two support counts (32 of 103 rows; 957 of 1,474 for v26). Every row's\n  change equals the fill's added layers.\n- **Logs:**\n  - **Most:** terrain cell counts, the extra ground-floor layer (0.058 m) in the probe's `[SUPPORT]` detail, and\n    diagnostic sets.\n  - **`original`:** the throttled first-blocked line names another query, now a measured obstacle.\n  - **`v26`:** a fixed-heading start check at 145.7° reads free.\n  - **`v18`:** two seed searches end on A*'s 0.2 s wall-time budget, and a later search recovers. The accepted\n    continuation is identical.\n  - **`v23_repeat`:** its first goal-neighbour search ends on the budget. That search already timed out in one of\n    v31's two runs.\n  - **`execution.log`:** build order only.\n\n  The explanations are in `log_difference_explanations.json`.\n\n## What K1–K4 show, and what they do not\n\n- **Shown:**\n  - The rule is implemented as specified: the oracle, the cases, the real map and both message orders agree.\n  - It frees both frozen corridor-entry stands on the first attempt.\n  - It changes no measured-obstacle verdict in the regression.\n  - Its other effects on saved states are the added support itself: longer continuations at the landing and onset,\n    support counts, and diagnostics.\n- **Not shown:**\n  - **Live behaviour.** A single physical trial is the next step.\n  - **Drop handling in a run.** It is tested by the synthetic cases and the node's hole checkpoint only.\n- **A* budget exposure:** the larger free search space makes some A* searches reach their 0.2 s wall-time budget,\n  as in `v18` and `v23_repeat`. Whether a search does depends on machine speed. On gpu5070ti, SCAN's container runs\n  natively rather than under emulation.\n{\n  \"parent\": \"v33\",\n  \"status\": \"unfrozen_candidate\",\n  \"native_build\": \".pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34\",\n  \"changed_files\": [\n    \".pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/grid_map.h\",\n    \".pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/scan_reactive_grid_methods.inc\",\n    \".pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/evidence_floor_fill.h\",\n    \".pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/repairs/2026-09-26_generic_occupancy/candidate65_evidence_floor_v34_identity.json\"\n  ],\n  \"native_parent\": \".pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/runtime/scan64_input_refresh_v31\",\n  \"diagnosis\": \".pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/audits/2026-09-29_corridor_entry\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
