{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '62,78p;130,166p' .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/scripts/run_local_episode.py\nsed -n '20,42p;48,82p;124,235p' .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34/src/plan_env/include/plan_env/eth_step_score_adaptation.h\"","aggregated_output":"def verify_integration_version(out, version=None):\n    \"\"\"Bind new runs to a frozen local integration snapshot, not a dirty Git tag.\"\"\"\n    versions = BASE / \"versions\"\n    if version is None and (versions / \"current.json\").exists():\n        version = json.loads((versions / \"current.json\").read_text())[\"current\"]\n    if version is None:\n        return None\n    if not (version.startswith(\"v\") and version[1:].isdigit()):\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected an integer integration version such as v4\")\n    manifest_path = versions / version / \"manifest.json\"\n    manifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text())\n    for name, expected in manifest[\"source_files\"].items():\n        if hashlib.sha256((PROJECT / name).read_bytes()).hexdigest() != expected:\n            raise ValueError(\"Version source changed; register a new version before running: \" + name)\n    shutil.copyfile(manifest_path, out / \"integration_version.json\")\n    return version\n\n        parser.error(\"long empty route requires geometry-only planning and PD stance hold\")\n    if full_building and not (args.geometry_obstacles and args.stance_hold and args.startup_mode == \"factory_pd\"):\n        parser.error(\"Full Building requires geometry-only planning and factory/PD stance control\")\n    if args.probe and extended_route:\n        parser.error(\"Use the separate control qualification before the full long-route trial\")\n    if args.stance_hold and args.scene == \"building\":\n        parser.error(\"PD stance adapter is qualified for explicit flat scenes only\")\n    if args.startup_mode == \"factory_pd\" and not (extended_route and args.stance_hold):\n        parser.error(\"factory_pd requires an explicit extended route and stance hold\")\n    if args.startup_mode == \"pd_stand\" and (args.scene == \"building\" or not args.geometry_obstacles):\n        parser.error(\"pd_stand is qualified only for geometry-only flat scenes\")\n    if args.scene == \"flat_static\" and not (args.geometry_obstacles and args.static_human):\n        parser.error(\"flat_static requires geometry obstacles and a static human\")\n    if args.scene == \"flat_box\" and not args.geometry_obstacles:\n        parser.error(\"flat_box requires geometry obstacles\")\n    if not 1.0 <= args.goal_wall_budget <= (1500.0 if extended_route else 400.0):\n        parser.error(\"goal-wall-budget exceeds the declared scene limit\")\n    build = args.native_build.resolve()\n    out = Path(os.environ[\"NEWTON_RUN_DIR\"])\n    if shutil.disk_usage(BASE).free < 10 * 1024**3:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Less than10GiB free\")\n    integration_version = verify_integration_version(out, args.integration_version)\n    for name in (\"source_sha256.json\", \"install_sha256.json\"):\n        manifest = json.loads((build / name).read_text())\n        if any(hashlib.sha256((build / p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() != sha for p, sha in manifest.items()):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Native identity mismatch: {name}\")\n    if not json.loads((build / \"build_result.json\").read_text())[\"passed\"]:\n        raise ValueError(\"Selected native build is not qualified\")\n    if args.geometry_obstacles:\n        identities = [json.loads(path.read_text()) for path in\n                      (BASE / \"repairs/2026-09-26_generic_occupancy\").glob(\"candidate*identity*.json\")]\n        if not any(json.loads((build / \"source_sha256.json\").read_text()) == identity[\"source_sha256\"] for identity in identities):\n            raise ValueError(\"Geometry-only episode requires its reviewed source manifest\")\n    for record in json.loads((BASE / \"setup/runtime_sources.json\").read_text())[\"records\"]:\n        if hashlib.sha256((BASE / record[\"path\"]).read_bytes()).hexdigest() != record[\"sha256\"]:\n            raise ValueError(\"Archived runtime source changed\")\n    epoch = time.time_ns()\n\nnamespace reactive_stair {\n\nstruct StepScoreParameters {\n  double expected_resolution_m = 0.10;\n  double critical_height_m = 0.26;  // Local V12 capability; ETH robot config uses 0.12.\n  double first_radius_m = 0.15;     // Includes the 8 adjacent 0.10 m PCT cells.\n  double second_radius_m = 0.15;\n  int critical_cell_number = 4;\n  double stair_label_height_m = 0.04;\n};\n\nstruct StepScore {\n  bool known = false;\n  double first_pass_height_m = std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN();\n  double score = std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN();\n  int critical_cells = 0;\n};\n\nstruct StepScoreResult {\n  TerrainSnapshot support;\n  std::map<Cell2, std::vector<StepScore>> scores;\n};\n\n// A nearest surface outside the existing step capability is not evidence of\n// this floor. Return -1 rather than joining unrelated building levels. Missing\n// or ambiguous association in a present cell keeps that local window Unknown.\ninline int nearestSurface(const std::vector<SurfaceCell> &surfaces, double target_z,\n                          double maximum_layer_distance_m) {\n  if (!std::isfinite(target_z) || !std::isfinite(maximum_layer_distance_m) ||\n      maximum_layer_distance_m < 0.0) return -1;\n  int selected = -1;\n  double best = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();\n  bool ambiguous = false;\n  for (size_t index = 0; index < surfaces.size(); ++index) {\n    if (!selectedSurface(surfaces[index])) continue;\n    const double distance = std::abs(surfaces[index].elevation_m - target_z);\n    if (distance + 1e-9 < best) {\n      best = distance;\n      selected = static_cast<int>(index);\n      ambiguous = false;\n    } else if (std::abs(distance - best) <= 1e-9) {\n      ambiguous = true;\n    }\n  }\n  return ambiguous || best > maximum_layer_distance_m ? -1 : selected;\n}\n\ninline std::vector<Cell2> circleOffsets(double radius_m, double resolution_m) {\n  std::vector<Cell2> offsets;\n  if (!std::isfinite(radius_m) || !std::isfinite(resolution_m) ||\n      radius_m < resolution_m || resolution_m <= 0.0) return offsets;\n  const int limit = static_cast<int>(std::ceil(radius_m / resolution_m));\n  for (int dx = -limit; dx <= limit; ++dx)\n    for (int dy = -limit; dy <= limit; ++dy)\n      if ((dx * dx + dy * dy) * resolution_m * resolution_m <=\n          radius_m * radius_m + 1e-12)\n        offsets.push_back({dx, dy});\n    const TerrainSnapshot &input, const StepScoreParameters &parameters = {},\n    const TerrainSnapshot *evidence = nullptr) {\n  StepScoreResult result;\n  result.support = input;\n  const bool parameters_valid = valid(input) &&\n      std::isfinite(parameters.expected_resolution_m) &&\n      std::abs(input.resolution_m - parameters.expected_resolution_m) <= 1e-6 &&\n      std::isfinite(parameters.critical_height_m) && parameters.critical_height_m > 0.0 &&\n      std::isfinite(parameters.stair_label_height_m) && parameters.stair_label_height_m >= 0.0 &&\n      parameters.critical_cell_number > 0;\n  const auto first_offsets = circleOffsets(parameters.first_radius_m, input.resolution_m);\n  const auto second_offsets = circleOffsets(parameters.second_radius_m, input.resolution_m);\n  if (!parameters_valid || first_offsets.size() < 2 || second_offsets.size() < 2) {\n    for (auto &entry : result.support.cells)\n      for (auto &surface : entry.second) surface.support = Support::Unknown;\n    return result;\n  }\n  // Unusable evidence scores exactly as without evidence.\n  const TerrainSnapshot *usable_evidence =\n      evidence && valid(*evidence) && evidence->frame == input.frame &&\n      std::abs(evidence->resolution_m - input.resolution_m) <= 1e-9 ? evidence : nullptr;\n\n  // ETH pass 1: maximum minus minimum elevation in the first circle.\n  // ETH skips missing neighbors. A present multilevel neighbor still needs\n  // an unambiguous nearby surface; do not join different building floors.\n  // Without one, the neighbour is a possible drop unless the surface evidence\n  // shows ground at this level there; that evidence height then counts.\n  for (const auto &entry : input.cells) {\n    auto &out = result.scores[entry.first];\n    out.resize(entry.second.size());\n    for (size_t layer = 0; layer < entry.second.size(); ++layer) {\n      const auto &surface = entry.second[layer];\n      if (!selectedSurface(surface)) continue;\n      double minimum = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();\n      double maximum = -std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();\n      bool complete = true;\n      for (const Cell2 &offset : first_offsets) {\n        const Cell2 neighbor{entry.first.x + offset.x, entry.first.y + offset.y};\n        const auto cell = input.cells.find(neighbor);\n        if (cell == input.cells.end()) continue; // ETH skips absent measurements.\n        const int nearest = nearestSurface(cell->second, surface.elevation_m, parameters.critical_height_m);\n        double height = 0.0;\n        if (nearest >= 0) {\n          height = cell->second[nearest].elevation_m;\n        } else if (!evidenceSurfaceHeight(usable_evidence, input, neighbor, surface.elevation_m,\n                                          parameters.critical_height_m, height)) {\n          complete = false;\n          break;\n        }\n        minimum = std::min(minimum, height);\n        maximum = std::max(maximum, height);\n      }\n      if (complete) out[layer].first_pass_height_m = maximum - minimum;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // ETH pass 2: max local step, count heights strictly above critical, then\n  // step=min(max, count/critical_cell_number*max); score=1-step/critical.\n  // ETH skips missing/invalid neighboring scores. The queried cell's own\n  // first-pass height must stay below the V12 critical value. This avoids\n  // ETH's soft score allowing an isolated too-tall rise.\n  for (auto &entry : result.support.cells) {\n    const auto &original = input.cells.at(entry.first);\n    for (size_t layer = 0; layer < entry.second.size(); ++layer) {\n      auto &surface = entry.second[layer];\n      auto &score = result.scores[entry.first][layer];\n      if (!selectedSurface(original[layer]) ||\n          !std::isfinite(score.first_pass_height_m)) {\n        surface.support = Support::Unknown;\n        continue;\n      }\n      bool complete = true;\n      double maximum = 0.0;\n      int critical_cells = 0;\n      for (const Cell2 &offset : second_offsets) {\n        const Cell2 neighbor{entry.first.x + offset.x, entry.first.y + offset.y};\n        const auto cell = input.cells.find(neighbor);\n        if (cell == input.cells.end()) continue; // ETH skips absent measurements.\n        const int nearest = nearestSurface(cell->second, original[layer].elevation_m, parameters.critical_height_m);\n        if (nearest < 0) {\n          // Measured evidence ground has no score; ETH skips missing scores.\n          double evidence_height = 0.0;\n          if (evidenceSurfaceHeight(usable_evidence, input, neighbor, original[layer].elevation_m,\n                                    parameters.critical_height_m, evidence_height)) continue;\n          complete = false;\n          break;\n        }\n        const auto &neighbor_score = result.scores.at(neighbor)[nearest];\n        if (!std::isfinite(neighbor_score.first_pass_height_m)) continue;\n        maximum = std::max(maximum, neighbor_score.first_pass_height_m);\n        if (neighbor_score.first_pass_height_m > parameters.critical_height_m)\n          ++critical_cells;\n      }\n      if (!complete) {\n        surface.support = Support::Unknown;\n        continue;\n      }\n      score.known = true;\n      score.critical_cells = critical_cells;\n      score.score = ethSecondPassScore(maximum, critical_cells,\n                                      parameters.critical_height_m,\n                                      parameters.critical_cell_number);\n      if (score.first_pass_height_m >= parameters.critical_height_m || score.score <= 0.0)\n        surface.support = Support::Unsupported;\n      else if (score.first_pass_height_m >= parameters.stair_label_height_m)\n        surface.support = Support::Stair;\n      else\n        surface.support = Support::Flat;\n    }\n  }\n  return result;\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/PLAN.md | sed -n '17,38p;160,199p'\nnl -ba .pipeline/experiments/2026-09-26_newton_stair_reproduction/versions/v34/PHYSICAL_RUN_PLAN.md | sed -n '14,48p'\"","aggregated_output":"    17\t  stairwell or opening edge, which PCT's inflation keeps clear today. The guard rejects exactly those (below).\n    18\t\n    19\t## Motivation\n    20\t\n    21\tThe diagnosis replayed v32's and v33's corridor-entry stands with the native planner and found two blockers in PCT's\n    22\tpinned navigation ground (`ground_precise.f32`), both turned into planning failures by SCAN's support query:\n    23\t- **Wrong-height cells (v32):** four corridor cells carry only the landing height, 1.419 m, where the floor is\n    24\t  1.561 m. Curve samples over cell (47, 41) fail the body-cell height match by about 1 cm.\n    25\t- **A narrow entry band (v33):**\n    26\t  - **The band:** the floor band is 0.8–1.0 m wide. It ends 0.5–0.6 m short of the wall that LiDAR measures, and PCT's\n    27\t    route runs 0.04–0.17 m inside its east edge.\n    28\t  - **Why it fails:** SCAN needs both footprint-circle centres over navigation cells with a floor layer. Headings\n    29\t    within about 45° of east–west are therefore unsupported at the stand.\n    30\t  - **At v33's start:** the rebound optimizer checks its first control points there at 0° (two coincident points)\n    31\t    and at −98.96°. All three are unsupported, so SCAN reports \"The robot is inside an obstacle\".\n    32\t- **Counterfactual grounds:** fixing the four cells alone unblocks v32's stand, not v33's. Filling the entry band\n    33\t  unblocks v33's. With both fixes, both stands plan on the first attempt.\n    34\t\n    35\tThe surface evidence (`raw_ground.f32`) is PCT's own uninflated selection of the same ground (traversability cost\n    36\t≤ 20, computed on the original PCD points plus dense mesh samples, `audits/2026-09-27_dense_static_sampling`). v30\n    37\talready lets it vouch for the ring PCT's inflation trimmed, in the step score. v34 lets it supply the floor itself\n    38\twhere the navigation ground has none at that level.\n   160\t## Claim boundary and residual risk\n   161\t\n   162\t- **What support now means.** v34 changes what SCAN treats as supported ground. Where PCT's inflation trimmed floor,\n   163\t  SCAN's footprint may now stand on it, and walls there are left to SCAN's LiDAR occupancy, as v30 already left\n   164\t  them for the step score.\n   165\t- **The drop guard's residual:** it reads only the evidence.\n   166\t  - A cell with no surface at its level and nothing below, but a surface above, is taken as solid. An opening above\n   167\t    ground that PCT's uninflated selection also excludes would be taken for a wall; LiDAR does not see voids.\n   168\t  - The guard covers the footprint circle: evidence cells within 0.35 m of the cell's square. A drop farther away is\n   169\t    not guarded by v34; there the navigation ground's own layers and PCT's inflation margin are unchanged.\n   170\t- **The evidence is not bound to the map** beyond frame and resolution (as in v30). In simulation both grounds come\n   171\t  from one Building; real-robot use would need both from the real map.\n   172\t- **Ground-floor additions** (14,458 layers) change support before the stairs too. Start and approach behaviour may\n   173\t  differ from v33's.\n   174\t- **The added layers are scored like navigation layers.** Next to a wall the step score may leave an added edge layer\n   175\t  `Unknown`, which blocks as before.\n   176\t- **Not addressed:**\n   177\t  - the 0° heading of coincident start control points;\n   178\t  - the replan start at the executing curve's end;\n   179\t  - the 1,000-replan limit;\n   180\t  - the tight corners beyond the corridor entry.\n   181\t- **Labels.** Only a physical run can support a navigation claim. A version increment is not acceptance, and v3 remains\n   182\t  the last accepted condition.\n    14\t- **Flags:** exactly `v33_historical_full01`'s, except:\n    15\t  - `--native-build runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34`;\n    16\t  - `--planner-config versions/v34/building_planner.yaml`, a byte-identical copy of v33's;\n    17\t  - `--integration-version v34`.\n    18\t- **Gates before physics** (the launcher, unchanged):\n    19\t  - v34's manifest;\n    20\t  - the records of `setup/runtime_sources.json`;\n    21\t  - the native build's source and install manifests and its build result;\n    22\t  - the reviewed-candidate identity of its source manifest (`repairs/2026-09-26_generic_occupancy/\n    23\t    candidate65_evidence_floor_v34_identity.json`);\n    24\t  - the scene inputs.\n    25\t\n    26\t  `hosts/2026-09-29_gpu5070ti/checks/p1_gates_v34.py` runs the same gates on the execution copy before the trial.\n    27\t- **The sync** (after the freeze):\n    28\t  - **What is copied:** the files the run loads that are new since v33's trial:\n    29\t    - `runtime/scan65_evidence_floor_v34`, whole, as scan64 was;\n    30\t    - `versions/v34`, without its `source/` snapshot and the contract's CMake build trees;\n    31\t    - the candidate identity;\n    32\t    - the derived runner and gate check.\n    33\t  - **The check:** every file in v34's manifest must have the same SHA-256 on both hosts before P1.\n    34\t- **Simulation only:** no robot and no training.\n    35\t\n    36\t## What is recorded\n    37\t\n    38\t- **Acceptance:** the unchanged Building review for the historical profile, and the local review.\n    39\t- **Navigation, v34's subject:**\n    40\t  - **The corridor entry:** does the robot pass it without a stand? That means turning into the corridor past\n    41\t    (−4.9, −3.4) to (−4.9, −3.6), where v32 and v33 stood. Where it stops, if it stops.\n    42\t  - **Progress:** the farthest route pose reached (index into the 631-pose route), the sim time at which the body\n    43\t    first passes x = −4.0 on the upper floor, and whether the corridor's east-end corner (route poses 200–207) is\n    44\t    reached.\n    45\t  - **SCAN's signatures:**\n    46\t    - v31's `trial_signatures.py`: \"inside an obstacle\", \"First three control points\", final-check rejections,\n    47\t      seed failures, replan cycles, the replan limit;\n    48\t    - the cells of final-check rejections (`versions/v32/corridor_entry_curves.py`'s method);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
